 "text": "Hello, how are you feeling? Of course. Celiac disease affects the small intestine, so it' worth being patient about dining out. Are you both open to cooking together, or would you rather shop together? Going for a while now. Pasta, bread, pastries, and some desserts, if glue free products are used. Also, many meats, fish, and some vegetables. Then look for sauces that are truly gluten free, or ask the chef to make one without it. Soy sauce itself is usually safe. Pick a glue free dinner that she knows she likes. Then immerse yourself in new recipes together. There are great gluten free cookbooks that show you' not giving up anything.",
